This page demos the editor support for templates, replacement components and
directives. Run the dev server once so the plugin writes its manifest, then open
this file with the PFM extension.

## Hover a replaced element

Hover the `##` of the heading above or the `!` of the image below. Each shows the
component that renders it, and go to definition opens that component.

![A penguin](/favicon.png)

:::Note[Directives are components](tone=info)
Hover `Note` to see its component, or `tone` to see the prop type. Press :kbd[F12] on
`Note` to jump to it.
:::

The frontmatter is typed too: {metadata.title} is a string, and hovering `title`
in the frontmatter shows its type. Opened {opened} times.

## Deliberate mistakes

This page builds and renders, but the editor flags two things on purpose.

- In the frontmatter, `draft: yes` is a string, and the guide template wants a boolean.
- The note below passes `tone=urgent`, which is not a tone `Note` accepts.

:::Note[A wrong arg](tone=urgent)
The editor underlines `tone`.
:::
